  "knownIssues": [
    {
      "severity": "Bug",
      "area": "Publish/Unpublish (Nine-Grid Completed list)",
      "summary": "Clicking Publish/Unpublish as a caller who is NOT the cycle's direct MyManager throws an unhandled server exception (HTTP 500 from Service/MgScanService.asmx/SetManagementScanPublishState) instead of a graceful authorization error. STILL PRESENT - reproduced a FIFTH time (2026-08-10 x2, 2026-08-12, 2026-08-13, 2026-08-14), byte-identical response each time, across three separate deployed releases now. Still not filed as an ADO bug - strongly recommend doing so at this point.",
      "reproduction": "Log in as the org-level account one level above the evaluator (not the candidate's direct MyManager), open Nine-Grid, Generate, select the candidate's cell, click Publish/Unpublish on their row.",
      "evidence": "Response body: {\"Message\":\"There was an error processing the request.\",\"StackTrace\":\"\",\"ExceptionType\":\"\"}"
    },
    {
      "severity": "Needs follow-up - now confirmed on 2 consecutive runs",
      "area": "Assessment validation banner not appearing",
      "summary": "Submitting the assessment with nothing answered still correctly highlights every required question client-side (30 of 31, correctly excluding the one optional trailing question). But the textual validation banner (server-driven, via the errorMessage observable set from the CompleteManagementScan response) did NOT appear within a 10-second wait on this run OR the previous day's run (2026-08-13) - both waited out the full 10s. The baseline and 2026-08-12 runs found it within ~1.5s. This is now reproducible across two separate releases, not a one-off - upgraded from 'unconfirmed' to a real finding worth prioritizing. The underlying code path (_unansweredMessage() in mgScanAssessment.js) still exists in source.",
      "reproduction": "Log in as an account with no manager relationship, start the assessment, submit without answering anything, wait for the banner."
    },
    {
      "severity": "UI change - test fixed, not a product bug",
      "area": "Personal Dashboard Report(HTML)/(PDF) buttons redesigned to icon-only",
      "summary": "This release removed the visible 'Report (HTML)'/'Report (PDF)' text labels from the Personal Dashboard's report buttons (now icon-only, matching the row-level icon style elsewhere) - confirmed via source (mgScanEmployee.html) and a live screenshot showing the redesigned dashboard rendering correctly with real scores/Nine-Grid position. The test's text-based selector found 0 buttons and would have wrongly reported the feature as broken; fixed to match by icon class (.fa-code / .fa-file-pdf) like everywhere else. Both report types confirmed genuinely working after the fix (HTML: opens a tab; PDF: real download).",
      "reproduction": "View the Personal Dashboard as the assessed person after publish."
    },
    {
      "severity": "Process finding",
      "area": "\"Add New\" button flake rate markedly worse this run",
      "summary": "The known 'lands on My Account instead of the new-candidate form' flake (historically ~1-in-6 attempts) hit 5-in-5 in a row when creating the standalone validation account, and also required a retry mid-batch for the main hierarchy. Widened the pre-click settle wait from 500ms to 1500ms, which fixed it immediately on the next attempt - consistent with Knockout's binding attachment now taking measurably longer after this release's changes (which also touched Starter.aspx.cs and session handling), not pure chance.",
      "reproduction": "Click 'Add New' on CandidateNew.aspx shortly after the listing page becomes visible."
    },
    {
      "severity": "Good (by design)",
      "area": "Kalibirity manual override (position swatches)",
      "summary": "The unauthorized org-rollup account's manual-override swatches remain correctly non-actionable (30s timeout, no data mutation possible) - confirmed again this run, consistent with ADR-001 authorization intent."
    },
    {
      "severity": "Confirmed release",
      "area": "Fingerprint check",
      "summary": "Manager/evaluator assessment side still renders 28 questions (not 31) - consistent with the 2026-08-13 release. This run's environment reflects 20 additional commits merged since then (Kalibirity grid-sync fix, pending-list duplicate fix, Manager report work, Personal Dashboard report button redesign) - all confirmed exercised in this pass."
    }
  ],
  "terminologyNote": "Reported roles are the feature's own two-role model ONLY - \"Manager\" (the person being assessed) and \"Director\" (their evaluator). A third org-hierarchy account one level above the evaluator exists only to demonstrate the Publish/Unpublish 500 bug in Known Issues and is not a timed role in this report."
